This difference appears to have been driven by higher baseline discernment in the control group. We did find that the mechanism proposed by the target authors—namely that the treatment impact on sharing intentions conferred by the accuracy nudge should correlate with the perceived accuracy of news headlines—was present in our replication. Our findings are thus in partial agreement with those of the target study, as well as with a recent study by the same authors that found significant effects of accuracy nudges on sharing intentions in three separate experiments, including a Twitter study (
Pennycook et al., 2021
).
